  "limitations": [
    "The raw 256-byte PCI configuration image or explicit unavailable disposition is supplied by the caller. This component performs no sysfs, kernel, VFIO, QEMU, hypervisor, or physical-device capture.",
    "The replayed provider fact proves deterministic binding to retained bytes inside the component; it is not a product capture authority, signed HostSnapshot publisher, external monotonic CAS, or durable repository transaction.",
    "A replayed PCI_FLR capability bit proves only that the standard capability bit was present in the retained image. It does not prove reset safety, reset cleanliness, reset execution, complete affected-function scope, driver restore, DMA quiescence, or device-specific errata.",
    "The factory hardware premise covers structural role, PCIe/FLR, typed dependency domains, IOMMU/physical/interrupt/reset facts, payload-root admin state, complete resolved owner-activation state, and fail-closed component gates. It remains a caller-supplied signed-inventory relationship, not product collector/publication/currentness or attach authority.",
    "The guest-resource-plan verifier checks only bounded canonical/schema/hash/upstream bindings and basic window order, alignment, non-overlap, and safe interval arithmetic. It does not discover BAR demand, run or prove the MMIO/BAR/RMRR/IRQ solver, independently prove allMandatoryResourcesAssigned, or observe QEMU/firmware realization.",
    "The operation-admission binding is permanently COMPONENT_STATIC_CAPABILITY_RELATIONSHIP_ONLY with productAuthorized=false and a closed blocker set. It is not proof of a SERIALIZABLE repository transaction, committed lease, successful CAS, journal fence, or side-effect authorization.",
    "Publication provider coverage, PCI binding bijection, capture timing, identity, and raw/semantic replay are closed normative x-qman rules plus schema-local constraints. Portable decision, rollback, and mutation verifiers now close additional caller-byte relationships, but this repository still lacks the target-Qman product publication transaction, authentic repository/CAS receipt, visibility proof, and delivery witness.",
    "Evidence-only raw-byte changes are intentionally excluded from topology semantics, but exact publisher currentness must still advance through the separate signed snapshot, authority-vector, and rollback-anchor chain in a product integration.",
    "No target Qman repository was available. Of 299 ordered integration-map items, 298 current-release items remain UNMAPPED/NOT_STARTED and the future IOMMUFD-cdev migration item is explicitly DEFERRED/NOT_APPLICABLE_CURRENT_RELEASE; there are zero target code or target test bindings, so no product collector, provider, publisher, planner, controller, repository, or side-effect call site is proven.",
    "There is no E3 end-to-end target-Qman execution, E4 physical qualification, or signed CaseCompletionRecord for C00-C03 or R03/R29/R38.",
    "This record cannot close C00-C03, R03, R29, R38, G1-G6, any product capability, qualification profile, support statement, HCL entry, or release gate."
  ]
